WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.320
The saved Week 15 plan asks you to connect incident systems, rapid triage, radio communication, changing patient priorities and an ethical debrief. The goal is not to memorize colors in isolation; it is to keep a shared plan functioning as the patient count and available resources change.
保存的第15周计划要求把事件系统、快速检伤、无线电沟通、患者优先级变化和伦理复盘连在一起。目标不是孤立背颜色，而是在患者数量和可用资源变化时维持共同计划。

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:42.552
The opened AET nine A lesson actually teaches Transport Logistics and Flight Physiology; that content has its own course lesson. Moodle labels the link as MCI, so the label and opened body differ. Here, the six-section MCI Response module is a topic-matched support source, not a claim that an additional nine A MCI body was recovered.
已打开的AET 9A课实际讲Transport Logistics and Flight Physiology，正文已另设课程讲解。Moodle却把链接标作MCI，因此标签与打开的正文不一致。本课使用六部分MCI Response模块作为主题匹配的支持来源，不声称另找到了9A MCI正文。

00:00:42.552 --> 00:00:59.472
A mass casualty incident is not defined only by a large number. BCEHS describes an MCI as a situation in which the initial response becomes overwhelmed; the relevant question is whether the resources on hand can manage the number and needs of patients.
多伤员事件不只由人数多来定义。BCEHS将其描述为初始响应能力被压垮的情形；关键要问的是现有资源能否处理患者数量和照护需求。

00:00:59.472 --> 00:01:17.136
A small rural collision may exceed one crew’s capacity, while a larger event in a well-resourced area may initially be manageable. The answer can change as more ambulances arrive, patients are found, hazards emerge or hospitals report reduced capacity.
偏远地区的小型碰撞也可能超过单组人员的能力，而资源充足地区的较大事件起初可能仍可应对。随着救护车到场、发现新患者、出现危险或医院报告接收能力下降，判断也可能改变。

00:01:17.136 --> 00:01:34.200
Think of the incident as several linked flows: information moves to command, patients move toward safe extraction and care, and units move only after receiving an assignment. A blockage in any one flow can create a queue or leave a patient untracked.
把事件看成几个相连的流：信息流向指挥，患者向安全撤离和照护点移动，救护车则需接到任务后再进入。任何一处堵塞都可能形成排队，或使患者失去追踪。

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:46.080
Your task is to keep those flows visible. Do not improve one local measure, such as rapid tagging, by sending people into an unsafe area or creating an unreported transport route.
你的任务是让这些流程保持可见。不能为了改善某项局部指标，例如快速贴签，而让人员进入不安全区域或自行开辟未报告的转运路线。

00:01:46.080 --> 00:02:03.456
The school index retains the A05 assignment. BCEHS now redirects A05 mass-casualty material to its Major Incident Management section, so the current role information and posted START/JumpSTART job aids are the operational reference used here.
学校索引仍保留A05阅读。BCEHS现已把A05多伤员内容转到Major Incident Management，因此本课使用现行角色说明及张贴的START/JumpSTART工作卡作为操作参考。

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:22.632
The AET course introduces useful concepts, but some older generic triage descriptions differ from the current local card. For practice, follow the exact BC tool and its 30-second target. Do not combine thresholds or actions from multiple systems because they look familiar.
AET课程介绍了一些有用概念，但部分通用旧式检伤说明与现行本地工作卡不同。练习时应遵循准确的BC工具和30秒目标。不要因为多个系统看起来熟悉，就混合阈值或步骤。

00:02:22.632 --> 00:02:40.392
The current BCEHS MCI page names an Incident Commander and a Triage Leader. The commander maintains the overall link with the communication centre; the triage leader uses the approved tool and reports the casualty picture while coordinating movement toward the ambulance extraction point.
BCEHS现行MCI页面列出Incident Commander和Triage Leader。指挥员维持与通信中心的总体联系；检伤负责人使用获准工具，报告伤员情况，并协调患者向救护车接运点移动。

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:57.072
A later ambulance checks in before receiving an assignment. Depending on the incident, command may assign treatment, transport, scribe or another function. These are tasks in a response plan, not roles to claim because you arrived first or prefer them.
后到救护车应先报到再接受任务。根据事件情况，指挥可安排治疗、转运、记录或其他职能。这些是响应计划中的任务，不能因为先到场或偏好某个角色就自行认领。

00:02:57.072 --> 00:03:25.344
METHANE begins with whether a major incident has been declared: yes or no. If not, the BCEHS aid calls for an ETHANE report. The remaining fields are exact location, type of incident, hazards, access and egress, number and condition of casualties, and emergency services present or required. State declaration status truthfully within your assigned role, and identify estimates and unknowns.
METHANE首先说明重大事件是否已宣布：是或否。若尚未宣布，BCEHS工作卡要求使用ETHANE通报。其余字段依次为准确地点、事件类型、危险、进入与撤离通道、伤员人数及状况、已到场或所需应急服务。应在受派角色内如实报告宣布状态，标明估算及未知信息。

00:03:25.344 --> 00:03:40.368
A report is not a polished narrative. State what is known, what is unknown and what would change the plan. Update after a hazard shift, new patient group, access problem or material change in available transport.
通报不需要写成完整叙述。说明已知、未知，以及什么变化会影响计划。危险变化、发现新患者群、通道受阻或转运能力明显改变后，都要更新。

00:03:40.368 --> 00:03:53.184
The purpose of check-in is to prevent a second crew from entering, parking or treating independently of the common plan. Confirm where to stage, whom to report to and which task you own before starting.
报到的目的，是避免第二支队伍脱离共同计划自行进入、停车或开始处置。开始前要确认集结地点、报告对象和自己负责的任务。

00:03:53.184 --> 00:04:09.888
When command or a function changes hands, summarize current hazards, patient count, work in progress, resource limits and unresolved decisions. The incoming person confirms the transfer; the team is then told which reporting line applies.
指挥或职能交接时，应简要说明当前危险、患者数量、进行中的工作、资源限制和未决事项。接任者确认接收后，再向团队宣布适用的报告关系。

00:04:09.888 --> 00:04:24.696
The triage leader’s current BCEHS function includes prioritizing patients and coordinating movement from the incident area to the ambulance extraction point. The triage pass is brief; treatment and transport functions follow the incident plan.
BCEHS现行职责说明中，检伤负责人要确定患者优先级，并协调其从事件区域移至救护车接运点。初次检伤时间很短；后续治疗和转运由事件计划安排。

00:04:24.696 --> 00:04:40.416
Do not turn the first pass into a long head-to-toe exam, an unapproved intervention or a transport destination decision made alone. A category communicates priority; it does not replace a secondary assessment by the appropriate role.
不要把第一轮检伤扩展成长时间从头到脚检查、未经批准的干预，或由个人独自决定转运目的地。类别用于传达优先级，并不替代相应角色的二次评估。

00:04:40.416 --> 00:04:57.384
For an adult who can walk on command and has no major injury identified in that brief sort, use the Minor branch and follow the plan for that group. Walking is a rapid branch, not a guarantee of health or permission to assign the patient an unsupervised task.
成人能按指令行走且快速筛查未发现重大伤情时，进入Minor分支，并按计划安排该组。能行走只是快速分支，不保证患者健康，也不代表可以自行让患者承担任务。

00:04:57.384 --> 00:05:21.480
For a non-walker, check breathing. If absent, position the airway as the current card specifies: persistent apnea is tagged Deceased; breathing that begins is Immediate. If breathing is present, follow the posted sequence: rate, radial pulse, then simple-command response. Do not add capillary refill or other thresholds to this card.
对不能行走者检查呼吸。若无呼吸，按当前卡片要求摆正气道：仍无呼吸则标为Deceased；恢复呼吸则标为Immediate。若已有呼吸，按卡片顺序检查呼吸频率、桡动脉脉搏，再看能否遵从简单指令。不要把毛细血管再充盈或其他阈值加进此卡。

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:38.832
The test is whether you can name the first decisive branch, not whether you can collect every possible observation. Once a patient meets an Immediate criterion, mark and move on according to the role and plan; do not spend the remaining 30 seconds proving the same category again.
检验重点是能否指出第一个决定性分支，而不是能否收集所有可能观察。一旦患者符合Immediate条件，就按角色和计划标记并继续；不要用剩余30秒反复证明同一个类别。

00:05:38.832 --> 00:05:54.024
If the observed information does not fit the card or you cannot safely interpret it, say so, follow the local escalation process and obtain the next authorized decision. Do not silently substitute an algorithm you remember from another course.
若观察结果不符合卡片，或无法安全判读，应说明问题、遵循本地升级流程并取得下一步获准决定。不要默默改用从另一门课记得的算法。

00:05:54.024 --> 00:06:19.320
The school plan explicitly names JumpSTART for the bus-crash scenario. Use the current pediatric card. When spontaneous breathing is absent, position the airway first. If breathing resumes, assign Immediate. If apnea persists, check for a pulse. The five rescue breaths apply only to that persistent-apnea branch with a palpable pulse, followed by a respiratory recheck.
学校计划明确把JumpSTART用于校车事故情景。应使用现行儿童卡：无自主呼吸时先摆正气道；恢复呼吸则为Immediate；仍无呼吸才检查脉搏。只有持续无呼吸但可触及脉搏这一分支才进行五次人工呼吸，随后复查呼吸。

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:36.264
The current chart uses respiratory-rate bounds of 15 to 45 per minute and AVPU-only neurologic sorting in the relevant branch. Follow the graphic in order; do not use adult rate thresholds, a full GCS or a remembered age cut-off as a substitute.
当前卡片在相应分支使用每分钟15至45次的呼吸范围，并以AVPU作为神经状态分流依据。应按图中顺序执行；不要用成人呼吸阈值、完整GCS或记忆中的年龄界线替代。

00:06:36.264 --> 00:06:51.792
The five-breath step is a specific JumpSTART branch, not a general permission to delay response for all children. It is not an adult START step. The local chart, training, assigned role and available equipment govern how the branch is performed.
五次人工呼吸是JumpSTART特定分支，并非对所有儿童都可延迟处置的一般许可，也不是成人START步骤。该分支的实施要遵循本地卡片、训练、角色和可用设备。

00:06:51.792 --> 00:07:09.600
If a child cannot walk because of developmental stage or disability, do not mistake inability to walk for a triage category by itself. Follow the tool and incident plan, including appropriate secondary review for a child who cannot communicate or manage basic needs.
若儿童因发育阶段或残障而无法行走，不要仅凭不能行走就判定检伤类别。应依工具和事件计划处理；对无法沟通或无法照顾基本需求的儿童，安排适当的二次评估。

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:22.800
A rapid category is not a definitive diagnosis, prognosis or promise of transport order. It communicates a priority under a particular patient picture, tool and resource situation.
快速类别不是确诊、预后结论或转运顺序的保证。它是在特定患者状况、工具和资源条件下传达优先级。

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:39.168
Different systems use different words, colors or criteria. The current BCEHS charts use the labels shown on those charts. Do not translate a local Deceased label into an unverified “expectant” policy or infer that a patient should be abandoned.
不同系统使用的名称、颜色和标准可能不同。BCEHS现行卡片使用卡片上列出的标签。不要把本地Deceased标签擅自改成未核实的“expectant”政策，也不能据此推断应放弃患者。

00:07:39.168 --> 00:07:57.360
The AET learning body discusses MARCH and lists examples of airway, breathing, circulation and warming actions. That is broader than the current BCEHS START decision chart. It is not a direction to perform every listed action on every patient during a primary triage pass.
AET教学正文讨论MARCH，并列举气道、呼吸、循环和保温措施。这比BCEHS现行START决策卡范围更广，并不表示初次检伤时要对每位患者实施所有列出的措施。

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:18.672
BCEHS describes immediate lifesaving interventions in the triage role as brief, with the current job aid setting a less-than-30-second target. Use only the action that the posted tool and your authorized training permit. The triage label must not be delayed by routine care or by copying a checklist from a different course.
BCEHS将检伤角色中的即时救命措施限定为简短操作，当前工作卡设定每名患者少于30秒的目标。只能实施张贴工具和获准训练允许的行动。不能因常规照护或照抄另一门课的清单而延误检伤标记。

00:08:18.672 --> 00:08:33.864
A patient marked Delayed who develops faster breathing, absent radial pulse or inability to follow commands may enter a different branch. The correct response is a fresh assessment using the assigned tool, not a defense of the first tag.
标为Delayed的患者若出现呼吸加快、桡动脉脉搏消失或不能遵从指令，可能进入不同分支。正确做法是用指定工具重新评估，而不是为原来的标签辩护。

00:08:33.864 --> 00:08:47.808
Reassess after a meaningful patient change, new information or a change in access, staffing or transport capacity. Keep the update connected to the patient identifier, destination and current responsible role.
患者状况、新信息、通道、人员或转运能力发生实质变化后，应重新评估。更新内容要与患者编号、目的地和当前负责角色关联。

00:08:47.808 --> 00:09:01.296
The tag and tracking method may be paper, a numbered triage device or an approved digital system. Use what the incident plan supplies; do not invent a parallel list that cannot be reconciled with command.
标记和追踪方式可能是纸本、编号检伤标签或获准的数字系统。应使用事件计划提供的方式；不要自行建立无法与指挥记录对账的平行名单。

00:09:01.296 --> 00:09:17.712
At every handoff, keep the patient identifier, current priority, movement, transport unit and receiving destination connected. When information is uncertain, state who provided it and whether it is observed, measured or estimated.
每次交接都要把患者编号、当前优先级、移动情况、转运单位和接收地点保持关联。信息不确定时，应注明来源，以及它是直接观察、测量还是估算。

00:09:17.712 --> 00:09:35.568
The current BCEHS Transport Lead job aid emphasizes ambulance access and egress, patients ready for transport, destination capacity, departing-unit records and avoiding ambulance stacking. Those tasks make patient flow safer and help keep the response capacity visible.
BCEHS现行Transport Lead工作卡强调救护车进出路线、待转运患者、目的地接收能力、离场车辆记录以及避免救护车堆积。这些任务能让患者流动更安全，并保持响应能力可见。

00:09:35.568 --> 00:09:49.512
Do not send every patient to the closest emergency department or let an individual crew self-select a destination. Follow the assigned transport plan and communicate a new capacity problem before it creates a queue.
不要把所有患者都送到最近的急诊科，也不要让单个车组自行选择目的地。应遵循分配的转运计划，并在接收能力问题形成队列之前报告。

00:09:49.512 --> 00:10:10.800
The A&P reading asks you to connect homeostasis and feedback with triage. A negative-feedback loop uses a response to reduce a disturbance, while positive feedback can amplify a change. In an incident, the analogy is that the system observes new information, takes an authorized action and checks whether the picture improved.
A&P阅读要求把稳态和反馈与检伤联系起来。负反馈通过反应减弱扰动，正反馈可能放大变化。在事件响应中，可以类比为系统观察新信息、采取获准行动，再检查态势是否改善。

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:25.896
This is a thinking aid, not a physiologic diagnosis and not a replacement for START. A fast-moving crowd, missing ambulance or deteriorating patient is a new input; the response is to update the shared plan and assess again.
这只是思考工具，不是生理诊断，也不替代START。人群快速变化、救护车不足或患者恶化都是新输入；应更新共同计划并重新评估。

00:10:25.896 --> 00:10:43.464
MCI triage can create moral distress because available help may not match every person’s need. The response is not to improvise a private ranking system. Use the incident’s approved tool, report what it cannot resolve and request the appropriate clinical or command decision.
多伤员检伤可能带来道德困扰，因为可用援助未必满足每个人的需要。正确做法不是私自创造排序系统，而是使用事件批准的工具，报告工具无法解决的问题，并请求适当临床或指挥决策。

00:10:43.464 --> 00:11:00.144
The school’s “greatest good” discussion should not be reduced to a slogan. Fairness requires clear criteria, consistent use, communication and re-evaluation; an assigned category does not describe a person’s value or make uncertainty disappear.
学校关于“最大多数人获益”的讨论不能简化为口号。公平需要清楚标准、一致应用、沟通和重新评估；分配的类别不代表一个人的价值，也不会消除不确定性。

00:11:00.144 --> 00:11:16.272
Stress, fatigue, family connections and visual chaos can narrow attention. A short pause to state the branch, a second-person read-back and an announced count can reduce avoidable drift without turning triage into a long examination.
压力、疲劳、亲属关联和现场混乱都可能缩窄注意力。口述分支、由第二人复诵以及宣布人数，可减少可避免的偏差，同时不把检伤拉成长时间检查。

00:11:16.272 --> 00:11:32.208
A difficult emotional reaction is not proof of poor character or incompetence. Use the planned debrief and voluntary support pathways; do not promise that a single debrief prevents later distress or require disclosure of personal details.
强烈情绪反应并不证明品格差或能力不足。应使用计划中的复盘和自愿支持渠道；不要承诺一次复盘可以预防后续困扰，也不要强迫披露个人细节。

00:11:32.208 --> 00:11:46.152
The AET module discusses limited evidence, human factors and the risk of both over-triage and under-triage. Avoid teaching unsupported performance statistics or claiming one tool is universally superior.
AET模块讨论证据有限、人因影响，以及过度和不足检伤的风险。不要讲授未经支持的性能统计，也不要宣称某种工具普遍优越。

00:11:46.152 --> 00:12:03.048
A rapid system is useful only when responders know the exact version, training and escalation path. When conditions are dynamic or the tool does not fit, use the applicable operational plan and ask for direction rather than silently editing the decision rule.
快速系统只有在救援人员知道准确版本、训练和升级流程时才有用。若态势动态变化或工具不适用，应遵循操作计划并请求指示，而不是悄悄改动决策规则。

00:12:03.048 --> 00:12:20.760
The school plan asks for rapid triage tags and an ICS radio report on Saturday, followed by a more complex Sunday simulation with multiple vehicles, changing priorities and command rotation. Practise the published 30-second target while respecting the exact local card.
学校计划要求周六练习快速检伤标签和ICS无线电报告，周日再进行多车协同、优先级变化及指挥轮换的复杂模拟。练习时应遵守已发布的30秒目标和准确的本地卡片。

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:32.592
The course can prepare your reasoning and language, but it cannot demonstrate your hands-on skill, certify your triage tags or substitute for the school instructor’s current station instructions.
本课程可以帮助准备推理和表达，但不能替你展示实际操作、认证检伤标签能力，或替代学校教官最新的站点说明。

00:12:32.592 --> 00:12:44.952
Teach the adult and pediatric algorithms separately from memory, then check yourself against the actual current charts. If a threshold or label differs, correct your notes before the weekend station.
先分别脱稿讲出成人和儿童算法，再用当前实际卡片核对。若阈值或标签不一致，周末站点前先修正笔记。

00:12:44.952 --> 00:13:00.288
For every patient, connect the tag to a responsible role and a next step. For every system change, say who needs the update. This is the difference between memorizing a triage chart and helping an MCI response work.
对每位患者，都要把标签与负责人和下一步相连。对每项系统变化，都要说清谁需要收到更新。这就是背会检伤卡与帮助多伤员响应顺畅运作的区别。

00:13:00.288 --> 00:13:30.000
Imagine several injured people outside a community venue, with restricted ambulance access. You have an assigned role, not unlimited permission to take over. Primary triage creates a temporary priority; the incident report describes current demand and access. Later, a patient becomes confused and the intended movement route becomes slippery. Keep those changes separate, then identify who needs each update and what action cannot safely wait.
设想社区活动场所外有多名伤者，救护车通道受限。你有指定角色，并非可以无限接管。初次检伤形成暂时优先级，事件报告描述当前需求和通道。随后一位患者出现意识混乱，原定移动路线又变滑。先分别识别变化，再确定谁需收到各项更新、哪些行动不能安全等待。

00:13:30.000 --> 00:14:01.224
The reading workshop supplies the complete connected explanations, including research, regulation, transfers, recovery and leadership. Use them to justify this case rather than memorize eleven unrelated summaries. The physiology reading explains regulation; the clinical readings test possible causes; the operational tools organize action; the professional readings help the team deliver and evaluate it. None replaces the actual adult or pediatric triage chart.
阅读工作坊提供完整相连讲解，包括研究、监管、转移、康复及领导。应以这些内容解释本案例，而不是背十一份互不相连的摘要。生理阅读解释调节，临床阅读检验可能原因，操作工具组织行动，专业阅读帮助团队实施并评价；它们都不替代真实成人或儿童检伤卡。

00:14:01.224 --> 00:14:30.264
Negative feedback opposes a disturbance, but compensation does not prove that the injury or illness has resolved. A confused patient with a high blood-pressure reading still needs assessment of neurologic findings, breathing, perfusion and the time course. Hypertensive emergency concerns acute organ injury, not the number alone. Consider other threats rather than deciding that every new mental-status change is hypertensive encephalopathy.
负反馈抵消偏差，但代偿不证明损伤或疾病已解决。意识混乱且血压偏高的患者，仍需评估神经表现、呼吸、灌注和时间经过。高血压急症关注急性器官损伤，不只是数字。应考虑其他威胁，不能把每次新发意识改变都判成高血压脑病。

00:14:30.264 --> 00:14:59.448
Choose measurements to answer the next clinical question without postponing immediate care. Explain the technique and relevant position, timing or equipment differences when reporting a repeat value. The pain reading adds onset, provocation, quality, region, severity, timing, treatment and the patient's understanding. A pain scale supports that history; it neither proves a cause nor replaces the patient's account or current observations.
测量应回答下一临床问题，且不推迟即时照护。报告复测值时，说明技术及相关体位、时间或设备差异。疼痛阅读补充起始、诱发缓解、性质、部位、程度、时间、已用处理及患者理解。疼痛量表辅助病史，既不证明病因，也不替代患者描述或当前观察。

00:14:59.448 --> 00:15:30.048
The literal CPSC pages concern transfers: assess the patient's ability, restrictions and tolerance, then choose trained assistance and appropriate equipment. A slow route is a resource problem, not permission for an improvised lift. Clear the path, agree who leads the movement, secure and use equipment as trained, and maintain communication. Do not transplant a hospital transfer checklist into ambulance equipment without checking the actual procedure.
CPSC字面指定页讨论转移：先评估患者能力、限制和耐受，再选择受训协助和合适设备。路线缓慢是资源问题，不授权临时拼凑搬运。应清理通道、商定谁指挥移动，按训练固定并使用设备，持续沟通。不能未经核实就把医院转移清单直接套到救护设备。

00:15:30.048 --> 00:16:01.632
The separately named fall section adds environmental and individual risk reduction. Wet ground, fatigue, cables, confusion and changing mobility can alter the plan. If a fall occurs, reassess and obtain appropriate help before continuing; do not automatically lift the patient straight back up. A controlled lowering technique requires training and situational judgment. Report a near miss as useful system information, not as proof that a team member is careless.
另行点名的跌倒部分补充环境和个人风险降低。湿滑地面、疲劳、电缆、意识混乱及活动能力变化都可能改变计划。发生跌倒后，应先复评并取得适当协助，不要自动立即扶回原位。受控下放技巧需要训练与情境判断。险些跌倒也应作为有用系统信息报告，而不是当作队员粗心的证据。

00:16:01.632 --> 00:16:41.400
The full emergency-care chapter extends beyond triage. In this case, ask whether confusion could reflect an injury, oxygenation or perfusion problem, toxic exposure or another medical cause before assigning a behavioral explanation. In poisoning, support immediate threats and seek substance-specific guidance. Do not induce vomiting or assume charcoal is suitable for every ingestion. Do not transfer an acetaminophen antidote to salicylate poisoning, or use a benzodiazepine reversal drug automatically for sedation. The reader names and explains these medication distinctions.
完整急诊照护章节不止检伤。本案例中，在归为行为问题前，要考虑意识混乱是否来自损伤、氧合或灌注问题、毒物暴露或其他医学原因。中毒时先支持即时威胁，再取得具体物质的指导。不要催吐，也不要认为所有摄入都适用活性炭。不能把对乙酰氨基酚解毒剂移用于水杨酸中毒，也不能自动用苯二氮卓逆转药处理镇静。阅读中点明并解释这些药物区别。

00:16:41.400 --> 00:17:15.864
Reassess deterioration even when an earlier tag looked reassuring. Distal pulses do not exclude compartment syndrome, and a remembered time window is not a reason to defer escalation. With suspected opioid toxicity, breathing and ventilation matter more than a pupil shortcut. For a distressed or assaulted patient, use safety, consent, privacy, supportive communication and appropriate referral; preserve options without imposing a universal forensic deadline or an automatic psychiatric diagnosis.
即使早先标签看似稳定，恶化也需复评。有远端脉搏不能排除筋膜室综合征，记住某个时间窗也不是延迟升级处置的理由。疑似阿片毒性时，呼吸和通气比瞳孔捷径更重要。面对痛苦或遭侵害者，应兼顾安全、同意、隐私、支持性沟通及适当转介，保留选择，不强加统一取证时限或自动精神科诊断。

00:17:15.864 --> 00:17:46.920
A delegation label does not remove accountability or give the recipient a new scope. Check the task, circumstance, person, direction and supervision. Is the recipient trained, available and equipped now? State the patient and task, the concern, the limit and when to report back. The receiver repeats the assignment, and the sender confirms or corrects it. A message sent is not proof of understanding, completed care or an accepted handover.
委派标签不会消除问责，也不会给接受者新增执业范围。要核对任务、情境、人员、指示及监督：对方现在是否受训、有空且装备齐全？说明患者与任务、担忧、限制及何时回报。接受者复述，发出者确认或纠正。发出信息不证明对方理解、照护完成或交接被接受。

00:17:46.920 --> 00:18:20.328
Interprofessional roles contribute different expertise. A transfer concern may need equipment expertise; a communication barrier may need an interpreter; ongoing distress may need a supported referral. Keep the incident reporting structure while welcoming those contributions. A structured clinical handover names the situation, relevant background, assessment and requested next step. Confirm who now holds the task rather than assuming that proximity or an electronic entry transfers responsibility.
跨专业角色提供不同专长：转移问题可能需设备专家，沟通障碍可能需口译，持续痛苦可能需有支持的转介。接纳这些贡献时仍保持事件报告结构。结构化临床交接应说明当前情况、相关背景、评估及所请求的下一步。应确认谁已接下任务，不能认为人在附近或填了电子记录就已转移责任。

00:18:20.328 --> 00:18:56.136
The pharmacology chapter explains United States medication-law history and the opening ethical principle of autonomy. Learn that context without treating a United States rule as British Columbia permission. For an actual task, check legal authority, service direction and available resources, and whether you are trained and currently competent. Record what was assessed and done, the response and unresolved concern. An information system can share data, but it cannot make an inaccurate entry true or replace a required live escalation.
药理章节解释美国药物法律沿革及开头的自主伦理原则。学习其背景，但不要把美国规则当作BC授权。实际任务需核对法律权限、服务指示、可用资源，以及自己是否受训且当前胜任。记录真实评估、行动、反应及未解决担忧。信息系统能共享资料，却不能把错误记录变成事实，也不能替代必要的即时升级报告。

00:18:56.136 --> 00:19:27.360
The mental-health reading extends care into rehabilitation, recovery, discharge and community support. Ask what matters to the person, what help is feasible and who has accepted follow-up. Recovery includes health, home, purpose and community, not only symptom removal. An online option may improve access but still requires privacy, suitability and an escalation plan. Do not promise a service, appointment or destination that has not been confirmed.
精神健康阅读把照护延伸到康复、恢复、出院及社区支持。要问患者重视什么、哪些帮助可行、谁已接受后续安排。恢复包括健康、住所、生活目标和社区，而非只消除症状。线上方式可能改善可及性，但仍需考虑隐私、适宜性及升级计划。不要承诺尚未确认的服务、预约或目的地。

00:19:27.360 --> 00:20:02.856
Evidence-based practice combines the best available evidence, clinical expertise and the patient's situation and preferences. A hierarchy helps assess a design, but a high label or a small p-value does not prove that an answer fits this patient. Shared decision-making explains options and checks understanding. A care bundle groups evidence-based actions. A bundle score can require every element to be present. That scoring rule does not authorize ignoring a contraindication or importing an outdated hospital intervention into field care.
循证实践结合现有最佳证据、临床专长以及患者情境与偏好。证据层级有助于评价设计，但高层级标签或较小p值不证明答案适合本患者。共同决策需解释选择并核对理解。照护组合把循证行动成组实施，组合评分可要求每项均落实；但评分规则不授权忽视禁忌，也不授权把过时医院干预移入院前照护。

00:20:02.856 --> 00:20:32.928
After the exercise, define the observed problem precisely. Was a route hazard unreported, a task not understood or a reassessment missed? An error can occur without harm; an adverse outcome does not by itself prove an error. Use a small planned improvement, observe the result and adjust. Distinguish having equipment, following a process and improving a patient outcome. Those are related measures, not interchangeable evidence of success.
演练后要准确界定观察到的问题：路线危险未报告、任务未理解，还是漏掉复评？错误可以没有造成伤害，不良结局本身也不证明有错误。采取小规模有计划的改进，观察结果并调整。要区分有设备、遵循过程及改善患者结局；这些指标相互关联，却不是可互换的成功证据。

00:20:32.928 --> 00:21:06.744
Leadership is not one personality or a universally best style. An urgent threat may require clear direction; planning and improvement benefit from informed participation. The leader explains the goal, makes safe escalation possible and checks that actual capacity matches the assignment. A brief sets roles and risks, a huddle adapts to change, and a debrief examines what actually happened. Psychological safety supports speaking up. Professional standards and the command structure still apply.
领导不是一种人格，也没有普遍最好的风格。紧迫威胁可能需要明确指挥，规划与改进则受益于知情参与。领导者说明目标、让安全升级报告成为可能，并核对实际能力是否匹配任务。事前简报设定角色和风险，短会随变化调整，事后复盘审视真实经过。心理安全支持表达担忧，专业标准和指挥结构仍然适用。

00:21:06.744 --> 00:21:36.312
Finish this case with an observable improvement and a named owner: for example, confirm the movement route before dispatching the next team and check whether the change worked. Offer support after a demanding event while preserving privacy. The leadership chapter also distinguishes management functions, planned change, mentoring and credentials. Learn those distinctions in the reader; neither a leadership certificate nor this course gives a PCP additional clinical authority.
以可观察改进及明确负责人结束本案例，例如下一队出发前确认移动路线，再核查改变是否有效。高负荷事件后应提供支持，同时保护隐私。领导章节还区分管理职能、计划性变革、带教及资格。应在阅读中学清这些区别；领导资格或本课程都不会给PCP新增临床权限。
